// Bank varbits, and the first varbits the mock's content has used at all.
//
// A varbit is a *named bit range inside a varplayer*, and every id here is
// OldSchool's, taken from OpenRune's gameval `varbits` group. The names are
// theirs verbatim, because the bank's own CS2 reads these ranges — a symbol
// invented here would name a range nothing on the client side agrees with.
//
// Which varp and which bits each one occupies is deliberately NOT in this file.
// The engine resolves that from config group 14 at startup
// (mock230_bank_varbit_resolve), so the layout cannot drift from what the
// client reads. Writing it down here as well would be a second copy of a cache
// fact, which is the failure mode this tree exists to avoid.
//
//   ./src/build/mock230   prints "bank tables loaded (N varbits, bank=1220 slots)"

3755=bank_leaveplaceholders
3958=bank_withdrawnotes
3959=bank_insertmode
3960=bank_requestedquantity
4150=bank_currenttab
4170=bank_tab_display
4171=bank_tab_1
4172=bank_tab_2
4173=bank_tab_3
4174=bank_tab_4
4175=bank_tab_5
4176=bank_tab_6
4177=bank_tab_7
4178=bank_tab_8
4179=bank_tab_9
5102=bank_showincinerator
5364=bank_hidedepositworn
5450=bank_side_slot_ignoreinvlocks
6590=bank_quantity_type
